The second constraint determines $\beta$: $E=\sum_i p_iE_i
 =\frac{1}{Z}\sum_i E_i e^{-\beta E_i}.$ Rather than evaluate this weighted sum afresh, differentiate : $\frac{dZ}{d\beta}
 =-\sum_i E_i e^{-\beta E_i}.$ Comparison with  gives $E(\beta)
 =-\frac{1}{Z}\frac{dZ}{d\beta}
 =-\frac{d\log Z}{d\beta}.$ The logarithm is natural because its derivative supplies the factor $1/Z$.

