Now set $x=\sqrt{\frac{\beta}{2m}}\,p,
 \qquad
 dp=\sqrt{\frac{2m}{\beta}}\,dx.$ The Gaussian integral becomes $\begin{aligned}
 \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}dp\,e^{-\beta p^2/(2m)}
 &=
 \sqrt{\frac{2m}{\beta}}
 \int_{-\infty}^{\infty}dx\,e^{-x^2}\\
 &=\sqrt{\frac{2\pi m}{\beta}}.
 \end{aligned}$

