p.src:
The entropy calculation assigned at the end of the lecture follows from $S=\beta E+\log Z_N$. Using Stirling’s approximation, $\frac{S}{N}
 \simeq
 \log\!\left[
  \frac{V}{N}
  \left(\frac{2\pi mT}{h^2}\right)^{3/2}
 \right]
 +\frac{5}{2},$ up to the subleading finite-$N$ correction. Restoring $k_B$ multiplies the right-hand side by $k_B$ and replaces $T$ by $k_BT_{\mathrm K}$. The result makes clear why the normalization factors that dropped out of the energy are indispensable for the entropy.

