p.src:
For an infinitely high atmosphere, $L\to\infty$, and $I_y(\infty)=\frac{1}{\beta mg}.$ The partition function becomes $Z_N^{(\infty)}
 =
 \frac{1}{N!\,h^{3N}}
 \left[
  \frac{A}{\beta mg}
  \left(\frac{2\pi m}{\beta}\right)^{3/2}
 \right]^N.$ Its $\beta$-dependent logarithm is $\log Z_N^{(\infty)}
 =-\frac{3N}{2}\log\beta-N\log\beta+\mathrm{const}.$ The first term gives the kinetic energy $3NT/2$; the second gives the mean gravitational potential energy $NT$. Hence $E_{\mathrm{tot}}=\frac{5N}{2}T$ for this idealized unbounded atmosphere.

